title: Shout it
golf: 30

Write `shout(word)` that returns the word in capitals with a "!" on the end.
`shout("hello")` gives `"HELLO!"`.
=== starter
def shout(word):
    ...
=== broken
def shout(word):
    return word.upper + "!"
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_shout(sol):
    eq(sol.shout("hello"), "HELLO!", 'shout("hello")')
    eq(sol.shout("Python"), "PYTHON!", 'shout("Python")')
